{
  "task": {
    "id": "Prob093_ece241_2014_q3",
    "spec": "\r\nI would like you to implement a module named TopModule with the following\r\ninterface. All input and output ports are one bit unless otherwise\r\nspecified.\r\n\r\n - input  c\r\n - input  d\r\n - output mux_in (4 bits)\r\n\r\nFor the following Karnaugh map, give the circuit implementation using one\r\n4-to-1 multiplexer and as many 2-to-1 multiplexers as required, but using\r\nas few as possible. You are not allowed to use any other logic gate and\r\nyou must use _a_ and _b_ as the multiplexer selector inputs, as shown on\r\nthe 4-to-1 multiplexer below.\r\n\r\n      ab\r\n  cd  00  01  11  10\r\n  00 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 |\r\n  01 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\r\n  11 | 1 | 0 | 1 | 1 |\r\n  10 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1 |\r\n\r\nConsider a block diagram with inputs 'c' and 'd' going into a module\r\ncalled \"TopModule\". This \"TopModule\" has four outputs, mux_in[3:0], that\r\nconnect to a four input mux. The mux takes as input {a,b} and ab = 00 is\r\nconnected to mux_in[0], ab=01 is connected to mux_in[1], and so in. You\r\nare implementing in Verilog just the portion labelled \"TopModule\", such\r\nthat the entire circuit (including the 4-to-1 mux) implements the K-map.\r\n\r\n",
    "interface": {
      "top": "TopModule",
      "ports": [
        {
          "name": "c",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "d",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "mux_in",
          "direction": "output",
          "width": 4,
          "signed": false
        }
      ]
    },
    "constraints": "SystemVerilog, exactly one self-contained TopModule DUT. Inline all helper logic inside TopModule; do not define auxiliary modules. xczu3eg-sbva484-1-e; 5 ns synthesis clock; simulator seed 1. No reference dependencies, hierarchy outside the DUT, file access, includes or DPI."
  },
  "sample_id": "9f31a35a-6bdf-4aa7-a051-f67a7f5a96f8",
  "variant_id": "C",
  "current": {
    "revision_id": "f62e2c19-1f68-4df8-8eb2-588dadbe2352",
    "source_sha256": "d9cc802c1fd0323a5bd37a7167b65d8fe6ef5f6a5a47cf723476f18e22593238",
    "source": "module TopModule (\n    input c,\n    input d,\n    output [3:0] mux_in\n);\n    assign mux_in[0] = c | d;\n    assign mux_in[1] = 1'b0;\n    assign mux_in[2] = c | ~d;\n    assign mux_in[3] = c & d;\nendmodule\n"
  },
